Subject: [PATCH] Authenticate and discover services from each title's metadata

Use Windows TitleId authentication for configurations without MSAAppId, and
retain each configured SISU client for newer titles. Discover the current
publisher service list under its own title claim, retain policy ownership,
and match WebSocket upgrade schemes without title-specific routes.

Scope cached tokens by account, title, client, audience and issuer; sign fresh
requests with the token's own key. Bound per-key authentication/discovery work,
retry failed discovery, and keep proof-bound user/XSTS exchanges signed.
No substitute title claim or generic-audience retry is used for failed titles.

Regression fixtures cover multiple synthetic titles, key/audience boundaries,
request signatures, endpoint precedence and concurrent cache work.

